# Topic ACL, read-only default: no identity may send a command to an Edge (acl-commands is the write-mode variant).
# Anything not granted here is denied, including #, $SYS/# and $share/...

# The Cloud: receives every Edge's telemetry and results, and is the only identity that sends telemetry acks
# (an ack makes the Edge delete buffered samples, so no Edge may write one). It has no commands write right here.
user iiot-cloud
topic read iiot/+/telemetry
topic read iiot/+/command-results
topic write iiot/+/telemetry-acks

# Every identity, through its username (= edgeId for an Edge): only its own topics.
# The secrets script never issues an Edge id equal to "iiot-cloud", so no Edge can own the Cloud's.
pattern write iiot/%u/telemetry
pattern write iiot/%u/command-results
# Kept on purpose, so acl differs from acl-commands only by the Cloud's commands write: with nobody allowed
# to write the topic, nothing ever arrives on it.
pattern read iiot/%u/commands
pattern read iiot/%u/telemetry-acks
